<title>USA: TABLE - First Home Bancorp Q2 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - First Home Bancorp Q2 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>PENNSVILLE, N.J. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.41		    $0.41</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>				3,804		    3,774</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses</p>
<p>				  100			100</p>
<p> Net			  1,122		    1,110</p>
<p>	   6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.89		    $0.84</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>				7,632		    7,507</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses</p>
<p>				  200			200</p>
<p> Net			  2,420		    2,275</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE:  First Home Bancorp Inc said its net income for the second quarter of 1997 included a gain on loans held for sale of $4,000 and a gain on investments of $37,000, as compared with a loss on loans held for sale of $61,000 and a gain of $77,000 on investments in the second quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1997 included a gain on loans held for sale of $7,000 and a gain of $91,000 on investments, as compared with a loss of $84,000 from loans held for sale and a gain of $113,000 from investments in the first six months of 1996.</p>
